Fresh Lo-Fi House

Lo-fi house came to prominence in 2012, when producers blended analog multimedia in their digital beatmaking. Nostalgic samples were pulled from 1980s-’90s analog tapes and online ephemera, with distorted kicks, fuzzy synth lines and emotive vocal riffs as hallmarks. Jazz, R&B, Balearic and acid house were all mined for their warmth. Today, lo-fi house artists are evolving by blending live instrumentation, hip-hop, garage and more into their template. Dive into this collection of lo-fi house tracks — featuring DJ Boring, Logic1000, DJ Seinfeld, Mall Grab, Sofia Kourtesis and more —  to hear the past and present of the sound. 
